      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per comment below, would change this from a boolean to an \"int usbFunction\" integer. Doesn\u0027t need to be in this CL.\n\nIt feels like what we really need here is to put it this information in the TetheringRequest, and have the TetherState or the IpServer store the TetheringRequest that caused the code to set up tethering. Until we do that, much of the code will not have the right information and will be forced to guess what USB function was picked when USB tethering was enabled. Currently that information is fetched from mConfig at various points in time, but I think that could be incorrect and out of date because mConfig could change at any time.\n\nExample:\n1. startTethering(TETHERING_USB)\n2. mConfig is set to use NCM for USB. Tethering starts NCM.\n3. mConfig changes to use RNDIS for USB. Configuration change happens.\n4. USB broadcast happens. enableUsbIpServing is called with isNcm set to true, calls mConfig.isNcm() which returns false. I don\u0027t know what happens at this point, but it\u0027s likely not what the user wanted.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 185,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 185,
        "endChar": 34
      },
