      "writtenOn": "2021-06-28T07:48:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it guaranteed that when the USB_ACTION broadcast is received, the interface has been created? If not, it could happen that enabling USB tethering is flaky: when this code runs the interface does not exist yet. In previous code things would work because when the interfaceAdded notification arrived, the code would create the IpServer. But that code is being deleted in this CL. Do you think there might be devices in the field running R that depend on this behaviour?\n\nThe kernel code appears to do do the right thing: register_netdevice is called when the gadget is bound, and I think that is a synchronous operation that has to complete before the function is actually enabled and the broadcast can be sent. So this *should* work...\n\nI wonder if on R we should continue to have the interfaceAdded continue to bring up the IpServer for safety? Or maybe just structure the code so that we can do that easily in case some devices have problems with the new code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 532,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 532,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "bfcb4cf6c56c0ca49c5bcec4c0f7002b6c24eaf1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
