      "writtenOn": "2021-06-28T07:48:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would rename to forNcmFunction to avoid confusion about what the boolean means. Just \"isNcm\" could mean \"this is TETHERING_NCM, not TETHERING_USB\" or \"this is FUNCTION_NCM, not FUNCTION_RNDIS\". Calling it forNcmFunction makes it clear that this boolean refers to the function, not the tethering type. We should rename it everywhere in this file.\n\nBetter yet, could this be an \"int function\" instead of a boolean? Perhaps not for this CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1334,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 1334,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "bfcb4cf6c56c0ca49c5bcec4c0f7002b6c24eaf1",
